---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="about"
  description="Fabian Hoeltke — working at the intersection of frontend, design, and AI. AI Engineer at Datadog."
>
  <section class="pt-10">
    <div class="term crt rounded-xl border border-line p-6 font-mono text-sm leading-7 shadow-[0_0_40px_var(--glow)]">
      <p class="text-faint"># whoami</p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <span class="text-prompt">→</span> Fabian Hoeltke — frontend <span class="text-faint">×</span> design
        <span class="text-faint">×</span> AI
      </p>
      <p><span class="text-prompt">→</span> AI Engineer @ <span class="text-accent">Datadog</span>, building the internal Cursor</p>
      <p><span class="text-prompt">→</span> I like tools that feel fast, look sharp, and quietly do the work for you</p>
      <p><span class="text-prompt">→</span> this site is one of them: it writes its own <a href="/digest" class="text-accent hover:underline">weekly AI digest</a></p>
      <p>
        <span class="text-prompt">→</span> elsewhere:
        <a href="https://github.com/fabianh001" class="text-accent hover:underline">github</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/fabian-hoeltke/" class="text-accent hover:underline">linkedin</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-faint">$ <span class="cursor-block"></span></p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-xs text-faint">
      psst — the <a href="/" class="text-muted hover:text-accent">terminal</a> knows more than this page does.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
